    "transitionPlan": "opens on v05's final frame (see \"Opening frame\"); the chip \"Next: why do two slits produce regularly spaced bright and dark bands?\" becomes the heading. On \"If light were a stream of particles\" the painted bench slides in as a strip across the top (laser module, slide holder with a coded double slit, screen carrier, on the optical bench; about 260 px tall) with a red beam to the screen. On \"screen\" a ghost overlay on the screen: two bright strips straight behind the slits (grey, tag \"particle prediction\"). On \"spaced\" the ghost fades and is crossed; the coded band pattern brightens; tag \"observed\". On \"makes some places dark\" one dark band highlights. On \"prediction\" a 3 s `Countdown` beside two chips: \"bright\" and \"dark\". On \"bright\" the first chip ticks and the central band pulses; red hand tag \"light + light = dark?\" beside a dark band and a red pen ring round the central band.\nboard change: two small coded waves (teal and violet) on a line. On \"crest with crest\" they align; their sum (ink) appears with twice the amplitude; on \"bright\" a red bright patch beside it, tag \"constructive\". On \"crest with trough\" the violet wave shifts half a cycle; on \"dark\" the sum flattens to zero; a dark patch, tag \"destructive\". On \"interference\" a chip \"interference: waves adding or cancelling\". Ink hand tags \"crest + crest\" and \"crest + trough\" on the two sums; ink pen ring round the flat sum.\nboard change to the two-source stage (tag \"not to scale\"): teal and violet wavefronts from the two slits overlapping; a probe point P on the screen. On \"slits\" two orange path lines from the slits to P. On \"difference\" a rose bar \"path difference\" between the two lengths. On \"Bright\" P sits at the centre: the rose bar reads \"0\" (live readout, 52 px, \"path difference = 0\"); P's cycle readout shows two waves in step; the central band lights. On \"again\" P slides up: the bar grows to \"1λ\" (readout \"path difference = 1λ\"); the cycle readout in step; the next band lights. On \"dark\" P slides back to \"½λ\" (readout \"path difference = ½λ\"): crest on trough; the band between darkens; rose hand tag \"half a wave behind\". On \"a whole number of wavelengths\" a chip \"bright: path difference = mλ (m = 0, 1, 2, …)\"; on \"a half more than a whole number\" a chip \"dark: path difference = (m + ½)λ\". On \"cancels\" both path lines to a dark band glow; a crossed chip \"dark = no light arrives\"; orange pen arrows along both paths into the dark band, hand tag \"both arrive\".\nboard change to the coherence toggle: left panel, the laser plate feeding both slits; wavefronts in step; a steady band pattern; tag \"coherent\". On \"same frequency, with a steady phase relationship\" a chip \"coherent: same f, constant phase difference\". On \"one single slit first\" a coded single slit appears before the double slit (grey, tag \"Young's arrangement\"), the curved front reaching both slits together. On \"Two separate lamps\" the right panel: two filament lamp plates (reused) each lighting one slit; the pattern flickers rapidly; on \"glow\" it averages to an even glow; tag \"incoherent: no stable pattern\". Hand-font tags: teal \"same wavefront feeds both\" on Young's single slit, grey \"phases jump at random\" on the lamps; red pen cross over the washed-out pattern.\nboard change to the derivation triangle: a large close-up of the two slits (separation d) with two nearly parallel orange rays leaving at angle θ towards a distant point (off board, tag \"screen far away\"). On \"direction\" a navy dashed straight-ahead line and the angle θ marked. On \"Draw a line across\" a dashed perpendicular from slit 1 to ray 2. On \"d\" the right triangle highlights: hypotenuse \"d\", the short side rose \"extra path\"; the angle θ at the slits marked equal to the ray angle. On \"theta\" the short side labels \"d sin θ\"; the equation strip writes \"path difference = d sin θ\". On \"centre\" t